#
# onyx_debug_reduction.fragment - trim debug/diagnostic features
#
# Tree: seventeen @ 6.6.142. The cost figures below were MEASURED on this
# tree, not carried over from the 6.6.82 one. Method: build the merged
# defconfig twice (with and without this list), run olddefconfig on each,
# and diff the resulting .config files. Both make and olddefconfig exit 0
# in every case, which is the whole problem: nothing here fails the build.
#
# Every symbol is chosen because turning it off does not resize or reorder
# any exported struct, so the GKI ABI is untouched.
#
# MEASURED COST of the full list: exactly 20 symbols are lost --
#   CC_HAS_UBSAN_ARRAY_BOUNDS  (hidden symbol derived from the compiler check)
#   UBSAN_ARRAY_BOUNDS  UBSAN_BOUNDS  UBSAN_LOCAL_BOUNDS
#   UBSAN_SANITIZE_ALL  UBSAN_TRAP
#   TEST_UBSAN  UBSAN_BOOL  UBSAN_ENUM  UBSAN_SHIFT  UBSAN_UNREACHABLE
# Nothing else. CONFIG_PROFILING, PERF_EVENTS, BPF_LSM, ARM_PMU and UPROBES
# all survive, which is the point. build-onyx.yml's reduction audit enforces
# this: it rebuilds the config without the list and fails the build if
# anything outside the allow-list moved.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GROUPS -- read this before editing
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The whole list is toggled by the `reduce_debug` input, and narrowed by
# `reduce_debug_group`. Each line below carries a "#@GROUP: <name>" marker
# and the workflow filters on it, so bisecting a suspected offender does not
# need a new fragment or a code change.
#
#   ubsan       CONFIG_UBSAN and its sub-options. 12 of the 20 symbols.
#   boot-debug  DEBUG_MISC, DEBUG_MEMORY_INIT, CMA_DEBUGFS, CLEANCACHE.
#   printk      PRINTK_CALLER, PRINTK_TIME.
#   rcu-bt      RCU_TRACE, BT_DEBUGFS.
#
# Why the groups are split this way: a boot that hangs on the splash screen
# is not a symptom any of these eight symbols explains by inspection, so the
# only way to find out is to turn them on and off one group at a time. See
# README-build-onyx.md for what has already been ruled out.
#
# Per-symbol notes, so nobody re-derives them:
#   DEBUG_MEMORY_INIT  memory-init sanity checks; diagnostic output only
#                      (lib/Kconfig.debug:876, default !EXPERT)
#   CLEANCACHE         Qualcomm tmem victim cache consulted by the page
#                      reclaim algorithm (mm/Kconfig:926)
#   DEBUG_MISC         depends on DEBUG_KERNEL (lib/Kconfig.debug:217)
#   CMA_DEBUGFS        debugfs for CMA
#   PRINTK_CALLER      printk with __caller__
#   PRINTK_TIME        printk timestamps
#   RCU_TRACE          RCU stall tracing
#   BT_DEBUGFS         bluetooth debugfs
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DO NOT ADD CONFIG_PROFILING TO ANY GROUP.
#
# gki-clo's reduction list did include it. Measured on THIS tree (6.6.142),
# adding `-d CONFIG_PROFILING` costs 10 further symbols on top of the 6 above:
#
#   ARM_PMU  ARM_PMUV3  HAVE_HW_BREAKPOINT  HW_PERF_EVENTS
#   BPF_EVENTS  BPF_LSM  UPROBES  UPROBE_EVENTS
#   GUEST_PERF_EVENTS  UID_SYS_STATS
#
# i.e. every hardware performance counter, all uprobe support, and BPF LSM
# disappear from a kernel that still builds cleanly with exit 0. That
# directly defeats the point of shipping BTF for eBPF: CONFIG_BPF_LSM is
# what CO-RE/BPF LSM programs attach to.
#
# The 6.6.82 tree measured 27 symbols for the same experiment. The count
# moved with the kernel; the conclusion did not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The stock device kernel -- the one whose config was extracted from the
# running system's own boot image, same tree, same clang -- has all of these
# ON, including UBSAN_TRAP and UBSAN_SANITIZE_ALL. A build with
# reduce_debug=false therefore matches it, and boots.
#

#@GROUP: boot-debug
# CONFIG_DEBUG_MISC is not set
# CONFIG_DEBUG_MEMORY_INIT is not set
# CONFIG_CMA_DEBUGFS is not set
# CONFIG_CLEANCACHE is not set

#@GROUP: printk
# CONFIG_PRINTK_CALLER is not set
# CONFIG_PRINTK_TIME is not set

#@GROUP: rcu-bt
# CONFIG_RCU_TRACE is not set
# CONFIG_BT_DEBUGFS is not set

#@GROUP: ubsan
# The sub-options are listed explicitly as well: the parent being unset is
# not something kconfig propagates to every child.
# CONFIG_UBSAN is not set
# CONFIG_UBSAN_BOUNDS is not set
# CONFIG_UBSAN_ARRAY_BOUNDS is not set
# CONFIG_UBSAN_LOCAL_BOUNDS is not set
# CONFIG_UBSAN_SANITIZE_ALL is not set
# CONFIG_UBSAN_TRAP is not set
